{"authored" [{"question" "q-11637" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,D=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,E=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $CD=DC={I}_{2}$\n- $DE=ED={I}_{2}$\n- $D={C}^{-1}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dda256f1c97457b101e926951c8e81554b09d8bc6ebcf8b818177ae70636939" "basis" 764 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11637" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- First, we check whether $CD=DC={I}_{2}.$ Computing $CD$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CD & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $DC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}DC & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is true. As a result, $D={C}^{-1}$ and statement III is true too.\n\n- Now, we check whether $DE=ED={I}_{2}.$ Computing $DE$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}DE & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ \\\\ -2 & ∗\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dda256f1c