my/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71818" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dda256f1c97457b101e926951c8e81554b09d8bc6ebcf8b818177ae70636939" "basis" 764 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71818" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dda256f1c97457b101e926951c8e81554b09d8bc6ebcf8b818177ae70636939" "basis" 764 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71818" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dda256f1c97457b101e926951c8e81554b09d8bc6ebcf8b818177ae70636939" "basis" 764 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71879" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & -1 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $AB=BA={I}_{3}$\n- $BC=CB={I}_{3}$\n- $A={B}^{-1}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dda256f1c97457b101e926951c8e81554b09d8bc6ebcf8b818177ae70636939" "basis" 764 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71879" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{3}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}∗ & -1 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{3}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is false. As a result, $A\\ne {B}^{-1}$ and statement III is false too.\n\n- Now, we check whether $BC=CB={I}_{3}.$ Computing $BC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & -1 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $CB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CB & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & -1 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dda256f1c97457b101e926951c8e81554b09d8bc6ebcf8b818177ae70636939" "basis" 764 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71879" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3522ef3314fed4769b534aa0321a492bb17fa48739bc3084445e43602ed2edec" "basis" 764 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71879" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dda256f1c97457b101e926951c8e81554b09d8bc6ebcf8b818177ae70636939" "basis" 764 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71879" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dda256f1c97457b101e926951c8e81554b09d8bc6ebcf8b818177ae70636939" "basis" 764 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71879" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dda256f1c97457b101e926951c8e81554b09d8bc6ebcf8b818177ae70636939" "basis" 764 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71879" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/t