$\n\nComputing $AB,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $BA,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BA & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B = A^{-1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/example-4499.json" "file_sha256" "f4a0e08c0f433b177315b28e7352fc9e0f4c7513750b020070c93de6e3de86f4" "basis" 764 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4500" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Using the method of direct verification, determine whether the matrix $B$ is the inverse of $A,$ where\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/example-4500.json" "file_sha256" "33ba0733f41977c7f7192db9951eab8a06aac4bf1d9dc2995f0760f244a45d30" "basis" 764 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4500" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we  check whether $AB = BA = I_3.$\n\nComputing $AB,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $BA,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BA & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B = A^{-1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/example-4500.json" "file_sha256" "33ba0733f41977c7f7192db9951eab8a06aac4bf1d9dc2995f0760f244a45d30" "basis" 764 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-7907" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=\\frac{1}{15}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,D=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $BC=CB={I}_{3}$\n- $BD=DB={I}_{3}$\n- $D={B}^{-1}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981514/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fd13b5eb1179276e70e193a252666c8458143b9ff33a4a91161432c91567cbc" "basis" 891 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981514/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-7907" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- First, we check whether $BC=CB={I}_{3}.$ Computing $BC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =\\frac{1}{15}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{15} & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{3}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is false.\n\n- Note, we check whether $BD=DB={I}_{3}.$ Computing $BD$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BD & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $DB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}DB & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is true. As a result, $D={B}^{-1}$ and statement III is true too.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981514/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fd13b5eb1179276e70e193a252666c8458143b9ff33a4a91161432c91567cbc" "basis" 891 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981514/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-7907" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981514/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c410cfe1cbce8ad8d3ea9b3510f6a3e7410b37a98890fcfb8401466d573874fc" "basis" 891 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981514/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-7907" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981514/state.json" "file_sha256" "2fd13b5eb1179276e70e193a252666c8458143b9ff33a4a91161432c91567cbc" "basis" 891 "verification" "/hom